// Broadside in the Ice: an ironclad shells a merchant steamer in a frozen harbour.
//
// Every hull floats on its own: no pins, moorings or joints. A body is lifted by
// the water its outline displaces, its dry hold included, so both ships ride at
// their waterlines and right themselves, and the ice floes (density 90) ride
// nine-tenths under. Scripted: the muzzle flashes and smoke, the shell tracers,
// the bursts, the solid shot's hole in the oil tank and the incendiary's heat.
// What follows each hit is the engine. The ranging shot splits a floe. The
// second shell holes the merchant's forefoot below the waterline: the fore hold
// floods through the hole to the sea's level behind her iron bulkhead and her
// bow settles. A solid shot opens the harbour oil tank on the ledge under the
// lighthouse; the oil pours into the sea and floats as a slick by the ice, and
// the incendiary sets it burning. The last salvo breaks the merchant amidships;
// both halves flood through their broken ends and go down onto the rock shoal
// with their iron ballast, her lanterns going out as the water reaches them,
// while the warship rides with her lamps lit. The sea is at 0 C, the floes -10 C.
[scene]
name = broadside in the ice
description = An ironclad's shells split an ice floe, hole a merchant steamer below the waterline so her fore hold floods, spill a harbour oil tank into a burning slick among the ice, and break the merchant in two; both halves flood and sink onto the shoal.

size = 1000 640
seed = 41
ticks = 1320
wind = -1

[legend]
w wood
m metal
t torch
s stone
b brick
k basalt
x glass
O oil
. air
C concrete
I ice body temp=-10

[build]
fill 0 624 1000 640 bedrock
fill 0 318 6 640 bedrock
fill 994 318 1000 640 bedrock
fill 6 330 994 492 water
temp 6 330 994 492 0

[grid 6 404]
